; ============================================================
; TITLE:    Rolling Two Dice
; CATEGORY: Mathematics
; LEVEL:    Beginner
; TAGS:     probability, random, arrays, histogram, animation
; SUMMARY:  Rolls two dice a thousand times and grows a bar chart of the totals, showing why 7 comes up most.
; ============================================================
;
; WHAT IT DOES
;   Two dice are rolled again and again and their total (2 to 12) is
;   counted. A bar chart grows as the rolls come in. Totals in the
;   middle win, because there are more ways to make them: a 7 can be
;   1+6, 2+5, 3+4, 4+3, 5+2 or 6+1, but a 2 can only be 1+1. The red
;   marks show how tall each bar "should" be, out of 36 equal ways
;   the two dice can land.
;
; HOW TO USE
;   Press Run and watch the bars grow. Change :rolls for a longer or
;   shorter experiment.
;
; CONCEPTS YOU WILL LEARN
;   * RANDOM to simulate a die: (RANDOM 1 6) gives 1, 2, 3, 4, 5 or 6
;   * an ARRAY of counters, one box for each possible total
;   * comparing an experiment with what probability predicts
;
; THINGS TO TRY
;   * Roll 3000 times with :tall set to 0.6 so the bars still fit.
;   * Roll only 36 times. Does the chart look like the red marks?
;   * Change ROLL to use three dice. The totals now go from 3 to 18,
;     so the array and the chart need more room.
;   * Count doubles (both dice the same). About 1 in 6 should be.
; ============================================================

make "rolls 1000
; how many screen steps tall a bar grows for each roll it counts
make "tall 2
; counts for the totals 2 to 12: an array of 11 boxes
make "counts array 11

to roll
  output (random 1 6) + (random 1 6)
end

; How many of the 36 ways of landing give this total?
to ways :total
  output 6 - abs (:total - 7)
end

to bars :done
  clean
  for [t 2 12] [
    localmake "x -330 + (:t - 2) * 60
    localmake "h :tall * item :t - 1 :counts
    penup setxy :x -200 setheading 0
    if :h > 0 [filled [80 150 230] [repeat 2 [forward :h right 90 forward 44 right 90]]]
    ; the expected height: ways out of 36, times the number of rolls
    setpencolor [220 50 50] setpensize 3
    penup setxy :x - 4 -200 + :tall * :done * (ways :t) / 36
    setheading 90 pendown forward 52
    penup setxy :x + 22 - 4 * count :t -222 setpencolor [60 60 60] setlabelheight 14 label :t
  ]
  setpencolor "black setpensize 2
  penup setxy -340 -200 setheading 90 pendown forward 660
  penup setxy -340 250 setlabelheight 18
  label (sentence [Totals of two dice after] :done [rolls])
end

to experiment
  for [i 1 11] [setitem :i :counts 0]
  for [n 1 :rolls] [
    localmake "t roll
    setitem :t - 1 :counts 1 + item :t - 1 :counts
    if 0 = remainder :n 50 [bars :n wait 2]
  ]
  print [total  count  expected]
  for [t 2 12] [print (sentence form :t 4 0 form item :t - 1 :counts 7 0 form :rolls * (ways :t) / 36 9 1)]
end

clearscreen hideturtle
experiment
